the target language is: lps.

the maximum time is 10.

the actions are:
    a discount starts for *a customer* with rate *a rate*; known as discount_starts.

the fluents are:
    there is a customer called *a name* with tier *a tier*; known as customer.
    there is an order for *a customer* with size *a size*; known as order.
    there is a discount for *a customer* with rate *a rate*; known as discount.

the knowledge base discount includes:

the text of the rule base is at "sources/discount.drl".

% Rule "Gold customers with a large order get the best rate"; salience 10 in the source (LPS has no conflict-resolution priority)
if there is an order for a customer with size large
    and there is a customer called the customer with tier gold
    and it is not the case that there is a discount for the customer with rate a rate
then a discount starts for the customer with rate best.

when a discount starts for a customer with rate best
then there is a discount for the customer with rate best.

% Rule "Everyone else with a large order gets the standard rate"; salience 5 in the source (LPS has no conflict-resolution priority)
if there is an order for a customer with size large
    and it is not the case that there is a customer called the customer with tier gold
    and it is not the case that there is a discount for the customer with rate a rate
then a discount starts for the customer with rate standard.

when a discount starts for a customer with rate standard
then there is a discount for the customer with rate standard.

initially there is an order for acme with size large
    and there is a customer called acme with tier gold
    and there is an order for zeta with size large
    and there is a customer called zeta with tier silver
    and there is an order for tiny with size small.

% Drools (a KieSession on the same working memory and steps) fired 2 rule(s) and ended with
% (its facts as this twin's fluents):
%   - customer(acme,gold)
%   - customer(zeta,silver)
%   - discount(acme,best)
%   - discount(zeta,standard)
%   - order(acme,large)
%   - order(tiny,small)
%   - order(zeta,large)
% The twin's final state under LPS2 (`lps state`) is compared with it by test_drools.pl.
